contain the zero vector.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "c5ce9ac0-bc5b-50bf-a92d-9c79b7832a98" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434598}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434600 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e5b2d85-4151-54a4-ac97-beef0024d1cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468076} {:answer/id #uuid "2c392c8d-2089-591c-a70b-c5983cd9d8ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468077}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468076} :answer-field/id #uuid "d486dc1c-3d30-5e4f-835e-f08717f52889" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468759} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "465a6071-09f7-5ac0-928d-43e875a45ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468078} {:answer/id #uuid "43d1ede4-b752-517f-859b-1a7a07ade02c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468079}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468078} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9c858f4-cbfb-5002-a626-7d8e4c6fc2c6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61b2f350-f63b-50a8-a1f2-5bd05dffb414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468080} {:answer/id #uuid "f07e9305-0844-5a74-9550-81a8ec3521c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468081}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468081} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fa3dc22-e26d-5b76-84a3-23639eb52190" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5e93e600-4a01-5ada-842d-9b175b57ee56" :question/math-academy-id "q-74217" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\nI. $A=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:1-x-y=0\\}$\n\nII. $B=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 1\\}$\n\nIII. $C=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:2x+3y-z=0\\}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $1-x-y=0$ since $1-0-0\\ne 0.$\n\n- The set $B$ is not a subspace. Indeed, the vector $u=⟨1,0,0⟩$ is in $B$, but $2u=⟨2,0,0⟩$ is not in $B$, since ${2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}≰1.$ So, $B$ is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- The set $C$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $2x+3y-z=0$ since $2\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 0-0=0.$ So $0$ lies in $C.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "e64a068c-ae0d-53dd-b1d8-27da858b1eac" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434599}}] :activity/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space: Geometric Interpretation" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434588}]}
